{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"entodermic-dizzying-pikeperch","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Land dependabot PRs #123 (actions bumps) and #124 (mcp 2.0 + ruff 0.16.1) through Gerrit\n\n## Problem\n\nGitHub is a read-only mirror: dependabot still opens PRs there (#123, #124), but they can\nnever merge — the updates have to be re-landed as Gerrit changes and the PRs closed by\nhand. Two are open now:\n\n* **PR #123 — github-actions group**: `actions/setup-python` 6 -> 7 (new pinned SHA\n  `5fda3b95a4ea91299a34e894583c3862153e4b97`) across 13 workflow files, plus a re-pin of\n  `pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish` v1.14.0 to SHA `dc37677b2e1c63e2034f94d8a5b11f265b73ba33`\n  (upstream re-tag; version unchanged). The change also updates the two `echo` allowlist\n  lines (the pinned-action identity allowlist) that mirror those SHAs.\n* **PR #124 — uv-lock group**: `mcp` 1.29.0 -> **2.0.0 (major)** — pyproject constraint\n  loosened `>=1.28.1,<2` -> `<3` in both the `mcp` extra and the dev group, new transitive\n  `mcp-types` package in `uv.lock` — and `ruff` `0.15.22` -> `0.16.1` (pinned in the dev\n  group; ruff is what `make lint` and the pre-commit hook run).\n\nThe mcp major is the risk: `rebar-mcp` imports v1 API paths — `mcp.server.fastmcp.FastMCP`\n(mcp_server.py:570, scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py:72), `mcp.server.auth.settings` /\n`mcp.server.auth.provider` (mcp_server.py:590, _mcp_auth.py:38),\n`mcp.server.transport_security` (mcp_server.py:512), `mcp.types.ToolAnnotations`\n(_mcp_models.py:287). Whether 2.0 keeps these paths as compat shims is exactly what the\ntest suite must decide; the upstream migration guide lists every breaking change.\n\n## What — two independently reviewable Gerrit changes, PR-diff-faithful\n\nBoth changes carry this ticket's trailer and land through the normal gate\n(`LLM-Review +1` + `Verified +1`, then Submit). Apply each PR's diff verbatim (`gh pr\ndiff N | git apply`), never retyped by hand, so the landed content is byte-identical to\nwhat dependabot proposed (SHA pins included).\n\n### Change A — PR #123 (workflows)\n\nApply `/tmp`-fetched `gh pr diff 123` onto a fresh worktree at current main. 13 workflow\nfiles + the allowlist echo lines. No source code is touched; the `Verified` CI run on the\nGerrit change itself exercises the bumped `setup-python@v7` on every job that uses it —\nthat run IS the functional validation. Risk note: setup-python v7 migrated to ESM and\nrequires a node24 runner (ubuntu-latest provides it); no inputs we use were removed\n(we do not pass `pip-install`).\n\n### Change B — PR #124 (mcp 2.0 + ruff 0.16.1)\n\nApply `gh pr diff 124` (pyproject.toml + uv.lock) onto a fresh worktree, `uv sync\n--all-extras`, then decide on evidence:\n\n1. **Compat shims hold** (expected path): the full test suite (`make test` — the MCP\n   surface is covered by `tests/interfaces/mcp/` and `tests/unit/test_mcp_*`), `make\n   lint` (now ruff 0.16.1), and `make typecheck` all pass — possibly after mechanical\n   fixes (new ruff rules, import-path renames with 1:1 replacements, updated\n   deprecation-warning filters). Mechanical fixes ride in the same change.\n2. **Breakage is structural** (FastMCP/auth API gone or semantics changed): do NOT force\n   the major through this ticket. Land the safe subset instead — ruff 0.16.1 bump +\n   `uv.lock` refresh with mcp kept `<2` — comment the evidence (failing test names,\n   import errors) on this ticket, and file a follow-up ticket for the mcp v2 migration\n   linked `discovered_from` this one; PR #124 is then closed with a comment pointing at\n   the landed subset + follow-up.\n\n`ruff format --check` may newly fail on files 0.16.x formats differently; run\n`.venv/bin/ruff format src/ tests/ scripts/` and include the mechanical reformat in the\nchange if so (it is what every subsequent commit's pre-commit hook will enforce).\n\n### Closing the PRs\n\nAfter each Gerrit change merges: `gh pr close <N> --comment \"<landed as Gerrit change\n<url>; GitHub is a read-only mirror>\"`. Dependabot sees the manifest change on the next\nmirror sync and stops re-opening.\n\n## Scope\n\n* IN: the two PR diffs, mechanical fixes needed to keep the gates green under the bumped\n  ruff/mcp, closing PRs #123/#124 with provenance comments.\n* OUT: any non-mechanical mcp v2 migration work (follow-up ticket if path 2 triggers);\n  dependabot config changes; other open dependency updates.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n* AC1: A Gerrit change with PR #123's diff (13 workflows + allowlist echo lines,\n  byte-identical to `gh pr diff 123`) is merged with `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`;\n  the Verified run executed `actions/setup-python@v7` successfully.\n* AC2: A Gerrit change for PR #124 is merged: either (path 1) the full diff with mcp\n  2.0.0 + ruff 0.16.1 and all of `make test`, `make lint`, `make typecheck` green, or\n  (path 2) the documented safe subset (ruff bump, mcp kept `<2`) plus a\n  `discovered_from`-linked follow-up ticket for the mcp v2 migration.\n* AC3: Both PRs #123 and #124 are closed on GitHub with a comment naming the Gerrit\n  change(s) that landed the content.\n* AC4: The decision evidence for Change B (test results under mcp 2.0) is recorded as a\n  comment on this ticket.\n\n## Verification commands\n\n* `git diff <base>..HEAD -- .github/workflows | diff - /tmp/pr123.diff` (byte-fidelity, Change A)\n* `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test && make lint && make typecheck` (Change B, in its worktree)\n* `gh pr view 123 --json state`, `gh pr view 124 --json state` -> `CLOSED`","id":"1dfd-063e-f341-48da","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Land dependabot PRs 123+124 through Gerrit (actions v7, mcp 2.0, ruff 0.16.1)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785710142255709001,"uuid":"64e113db-92fb-4ad9-8fb4-766ea3eed2ae"}